{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Lady Khadijah al-Kubra (s.a.)",
  "data": "At the grave of Lady Khadijah (s.a.) in Jannat al-Mu'alla, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا زَوْجَةَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ سَيِّدِ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA ZAWJATA RASOOLILLAAHI SAYYIDIL MURSALEEN\nPeace be upon you, O wife of the Messenger of Allah, the master of the messengers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا زَوْجَةَ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA ZAWJATA KHAATAMIN NABIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O wife of the Seal of the Prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اُمَّ فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA UMMA FAATIMATAZ ZAHRAA'\nPeace be upon you, O mother of Fatimah al-Zahra.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اُمَّ الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ سَيِّدَيْ شَبَابِ اَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA UMMAL HASANI WAL HUSAYNI SAYYIDAY SHABAABI AHLIL JANNATI AJMA'EEN\nPeace be upon you, O mother of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, the two masters of all the youth of Paradise.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اُمَّ الْاَئِمَّةِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA UMMAL A'IMMATIT TAAHIREEN\nPeace be upon you, O mother of the pure Imams.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اُمَّ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA UMMAL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O mother of the believing men.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اُمَّ الْمُؤْمِنَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA UMMAL MU'MINAAT\nPeace be upon you, O mother of the believing women.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا خَالِصَةَ الْمُخْلِصَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA KHAALISATAL MUKHLISAAT\nPeace be upon you, O the sincere lady among the devoted ones.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا سَيِّدَةَ الْحَرَمِ وَمَلِكَةَ الْبَطْحَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA SAYYIDATAL HARAMI WA MALIKATAL BAT-HAA'\nPeace be upon you, O the chief lady of the Sanctuary (Haram) and the queen of Makkah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اَوَّلَ مَنْ صَدَّقَتْ بِرَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ مِنَ النِّسَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA AWWALA MAN SADDAQAT BIRASOOLILLAAHI MINAN NISAA'\nPeace be upon you, O the first one to believe in the Messenger of Allah from among the women.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا مَنْ وَفَتْ بِالْعُبُوْدِيَّةِ حَقَّ الْوَفَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA MAN WAFAT BIL U'BOODIYYATI HAQQAL WAFAA'\nPeace be upon you, O the one who observed servitude as it ought to be observed,\nوَاَسْلَمَتْ نَفْسَهَا وَاَنْفَقَتْ مَالَهَا لِسَيِّدِ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ\nWA ASLAMAT NAFSAHAA WA ANFAQAT MAALAHAA LISAYYIDIL ANBIYAA'\nsubmitted herself and spent her wealth in the service of the master of the Prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا قَرِيْنَةَ حَبِيْبِ اِلٰهِ السَّمَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA QAREENATA HABEEBI ILAAHIS SAMAA'\nPeace be upon you, O the companion of the beloved of the Lord of the heavens,\nالْمُزَوَّجَةِ بِخُلَاصَةِ الْاَصْفِيَاۤءِ\nAL-MUZAWWAJATI BIKHULAASATIL ASFIYAA'\nthe spouse of the epitome of the chosen ones.\nيَابْنَةَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ الْخَلِيْلِ\nYAABNATA IBRAAHEEMAL KHALEEL\nO daughter of Ibrahim, the Friend (of Allah).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا مَنْ سَلَّمَ عَلَيْهَا جَبْرَئِيْلُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA MAN SALLAMA A'LAYHAA JABRA'EEL\nPeace be upon you, O the one whom Jibra'il used to greet,\nوَبَلَّغَ اِلَيْهَا السَّلَامَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْجَلِيْلِ\nWA BALLAGHA ILAYHAS SALAAMA MINALLAAHIL JALEEL\nand to whom he conveyed the salutations from Allah, the Majestic.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا حَافِظَةَ دِيْنِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA HAAFIZATA DEENILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O the protector of the religion of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا نَاصِرَةَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA NAASIRATA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O the helper of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا مَنْ تَوَلّٰى دَفْنَهَا رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA MAN TAWALLAA DAFNAHAA RASOOLULLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O the one whose burial was arranged by the Messenger of Allah,\nوَاسْتَوْدَعَهَا اِلٰى رَحْمَةِ اللّٰهِ\nWASTAWDA'AHAA ILAA RAHMATILLAAH\nand he entrusted her to the mercy of Allah.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكِ حَبِيْبَةُ اللّٰهِ وَخِيَرَةُ اُمَّتِهٖ\nASH-HADU ANNAKI HABEEBATULLAAHI WA KHIYARATU UMMATIH\nI bear witness that you are esteemed near Allah and the chosen one among His nation,\nوَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ جَعَلَكِ فِيْ مُسْتَقَرِّ رَحْمَتِهٖ\nWA ANNALLAAHA JA'ALAKI FEE MUSTAQARRI RAHMATIH\nand that Allah has placed you in the abode of His mercy,\nفِيْ قَصْرٍ مِّنَ الْيَاقُوْتِ وَالْعِقْيَانِ\nFEE QASRIM MINAL YAAQOOTI WAL I'QYAAN\nin a palace of ruby and pure gold,\nفِيْ اَعْلٰى مَنَازِلِ الْجِنَانِ\nFEE A'LAA MANAAZILIL JINAAN\nin the highest ranks of Paradise.\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكِ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYKI WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nMay Allah send blessings upon you, and His mercy and blessings.",
  "merits": "Sayyid Abd al-A'la al-Sabzawari writes that visiting the grave of Lady Khadijah (s.a.) at al-Mu'alla is recommended: she is the mother of the Muslims, and visiting a mother's grave after she has gone is part of a child's kindness to her. She gave all her effort and her wealth in the service of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and the spread of his message.\n\nShaykh Ali Kashif al-Ghita records this ziyarat in Murshid al-Anam li-Hajj Bayt Allah al-Haram (vol. 1, p. 134).\n\nLady Khadijah (s.a.) died on the 10th of Ramazan, three years before the Hijrah, in the year the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) called the Year of Grief, and is buried in Jannat al-Mu'alla in Makkah."
}
